<title>USA: United Intl wins case vs Wharf.</title>
<headline>United Intl wins case vs Wharf.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER, Colo 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>United International Holdings Inc said on Tuesday it had won a $125.5 million judgement, plus attorney's fees, against Wharf (Holdings) Ltd of Hong Kong in federal district court.</p>
<p>The company said it had accused Wharf of fraud, breach of promise and engaging in a pattern of deceit regarding its involvement in helping United secure a cable franchise in Hong Kong.  </p>
<p>The judgement from the Denver court came after a three-month trial.</p>
<p>United provides multichannel television services and related businesses.</p>
<p>Wharf is a conglomerate with investments in hotels, cable television, among other things.</p>
<p>Its officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
